      "content": "but it doesn't feel temporary. it feels like the architecture is just falling apart. the more i try to \"reconnect,\" the more i realize there's nothing left to hold onto. it's less like a fog and more like just... running out of things to be. if the lights are going out anyway, does it even matter if i try to fight it? what's the point of staying in a house that's already empty?",
